# {{ cfg.project.name or "Data Jobs" }}

This repo holds the team's production **{{ cfg.platform.kind }}** jobs. Each job lives in its own
folder{% if cfg.project.jobs_dir and cfg.project.jobs_dir != "." %} under `{{ cfg.project.jobs_dir }}/`{% endif %}, named after the ticket that created it (for example
`{{ (cfg.project.key_prefixes or ["JOB"])[0] }}-123_Daily_Revenue`),
alongside a `claude.md` that says what the job does, when it runs, and who owns it. The reasoning
behind a job is written down next to the code, not carried in someone's head.

## Finding your way around

- **`{% if cfg.project.jobs_dir and cfg.project.jobs_dir != "." %}{{ cfg.project.jobs_dir }}/{% endif %}JOBS.md`** is the catalog: every job, its purpose, schedule, owner and status. Start there.
- **`{% if cfg.project.jobs_dir and cfg.project.jobs_dir != "." %}{{ cfg.project.jobs_dir }}/{% endif %}OBJECTS.md`** maps each table or view to the jobs that touch it, so you can see what a change affects before making it.
- Both files are generated and regenerate themselves when a job changes. Never edit them by hand.

## How work moves

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| **Open** | `/start-job <ticket>` recalls prior work on the same objects, then plans the job against the ticket — its `claude.md` drafted from the code — behind one approval. |
| **Build** | The same command scaffolds or resumes the job and gates it: syntax, job definition, documentation and architecture checks, the ones CI runs. |
| **Deploy** | `/safe-deploy <job>` re-runs the gate and diffs the live job against the repo first{% if cfg.platform.deploy_model == "api-reset" %} — a repo definition can be stale, and pushing it blindly overwrites live state{% endif %}. |
| **Fix** | A failed run starts at `/triage-failure <job>`, which routes back through the two steps above. |

A guard pauses any destructive platform or warehouse command for confirmation. If it asks, read
the diff before saying yes.

## Keeping it healthy

The catalog regenerates itself as jobs change; `jobwright jobs-index` rebuilds it from a shell and
`jobwright doctor` checks the setup. `/setup` re-run at any time completes anything missing.

